From 473a820f5bde1e72f2a6dc6463aa1af91f77384b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:11:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] PLL parsimony: compile fastDNAparsimony.c with -mpopcnt
 on x86-64

The parsimony kernels that build IQ-TREE's starting trees are
integer-only and sum __builtin_popcount over every vector they touch;
in the generic -msse3 build that is a bit-twiddling sequence per
64-bit word. With POPCNT it is one instruction. Scores, and so the
starting trees, cannot change.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QBkV69MxCAg5qwKtaWSJ2d
---
 pll/CMakeLists.txt | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pll/CMakeLists.txt b/pll/CMakeLists.txt
index a04837b0..51f81dad 100644
--- a/pll/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/pll/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -65,3 +65,9 @@ add_library(pll
   treeIO.c
   utils.c)
 endif()
+
+# The parsimony kernels are integer-only and spend much of their time in
+# __builtin_popcount, which without POPCNT compiles to a bit-twiddling sequence.
+if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "x86_64|AMD64" AND NOT IQTREE_FLAGS MATCHES "novx")
+    set_source_files_properties(fastDNAparsimony.c PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS "-mpopcnt")
+endif()
-- 
