From 7a43616e5cd1283764401c912717f76e49a7ff65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Kernels: capture the Derv packet's inputs by value

The packet lambda only writes its sums (parameters) and arrays reached
through pointers; capture the other locals by value so the pattern loop
does not reload them through the closure. A non-mutable lambda cannot
assign a by-value capture, so the compiler confirms none is written.
The variable-length arrays stay by reference.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QBkV69MxCAg5qwKtaWSJ2d
---
 tree/phylokernelnew.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tree/phylokernelnew.h b/tree/phylokernelnew.h
index 00adb914..0e4b59ba 100644
--- a/tree/phylokernelnew.h
+++ b/tree/phylokernelnew.h
@@ -2446,7 +2446,7 @@ void PhyloTree::computeLikelihoodDervGenericSIMD(PhyloNeighbor *dad_branch, Phyl
     double all_lh(0.0), all_df(0.0), all_ddf(0.0), all_prob_const(0.0), all_df_const(0.0), all_ddf_const(0.0);
     // One packet. The sums are parameters so that inside the OpenMP loop they bind to the
     // thread's reduction copies.
-    auto derv_packet = [&](int packet_id, double &all_lh, double &all_df, double &all_ddf,
+    auto derv_packet = [=, &cat_rate, &cat_prop, &mix_addr_nstates_malign, &mix_addr_malign, &cat_id](int packet_id, double &all_lh, double &all_df, double &all_ddf,
                            double &all_prob_const, double &all_df_const, double &all_ddf_const) {
